 also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two specimens  Labeled  left breast  short superior  long lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm skin ellipse excised a depth of 0 3cm and containing a 2 5cm well healed linear scar  There is a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a double stitch designating the inferior   deep   margin  The anterior aspect is inked in blue while the posterior is inked in black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity with a hemorrhagic  fibrous tract extending to the skin ellipse  There is a firm  tan white  hemorrhagic nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm present in the posterior wall of the biopsy cavity  The cavity is 0 6cm from the posterior inferior margin and 0 6cm from the anterior margin  The rim of stellate fibrosis extends to the posterosuperior and posteroinferior margins  Apparently contiguous with the nodule in the biopsy cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm well circumscribed soft tissue mass with a tan yellow  hemorrhagic rim and brown  variegated center  This nodule is present at the anterior margin and 0 5cm from the posterior margin  Representative sections are taken lateral to medial as follows  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity  nearest  posterior  margin  B  Inferior biopsy cavity  C D  Superior aspect biopsy cavity  E  Fibrous tract to skin from biopsy cav