 this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm skin ellipse and unremarkable nipple areolar complex  There is a suture designating the superior aspect  There is a 7 0cm horizontal  linear  well healed scar present 4 5cm superior to the nipple  The excised surface is inked black  with the anterior surface overinked red  Cross sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm biopsy cavity 1 0cm beneath the skin  beneath the scar  and abutting the deep margin along a broad front  The biopsy cavity is lined by white fibrous tissue with a few fibrous strands extending into the adjacent fat  There is also fat necrosis surrounding the biopsy cavity site  Tissue away from the biopsy cavity is mixed white fibrous parenchyma and fatty tissue  No discrete lesions are identified  Section code  A  Biopsy cavity with deep margin B F  Sections of biopsy cavity from inferior to superior G H  Representative sections of tissue away from biopsy cavity  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
