ace of the specimen mentioned above  The biopsy cavity is surrounded by a rim of fibrofatty tissue  which varies in thickness from 0 3cm to 2cm  The wall of the biopsy cavity is granular and in the deep mid portion of the specimen there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm  white nodule  as well as focal nodularity associated with the biopsy cavity  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 0cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  One surface of this tissue is hemorrhagic and appears similar to the inside of the biopsy cavity  The specimen is inked blue over the portion resembling the biopsy cavity and black over the remainder of the surface and serially sectioned to reveal two  white  0 4cm in diameter nodules  grossly abutting the black inked resection margin  Received designated  Right axilla nodes  is a 88 gram  9 x 8 x 4cm axillary node dissection  No nodes are grossly positive  Section Code  A  lateral margin en face  B  lateral deep margin  radial  C  deep  mid margin with firm  white nodule  D  mid inferior margin  E  deep and slightly medial  F  deep mid  G  deep  slightly superior  nodular associated with biopsy cavity wall  H  nodularity near medial aspect  I  medial margin en face  J  skin with scar  K  representative biopsy cavity  L  rest of the nodule submitted in C  M  representative of deep biopsy cavity  N Q  Representative separately submitted  Superior margin  including two nodules  R U  lymph nodes  S  two sections of one lymph node  one section showing a 0 2cm yellowish area in the center of the node  Resident  James Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART A  BREAST WIDE EXCISION  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLA NODE  RIGHT  PART C  SUPERIOR MARGIN   report_end  , Unchecked.
