Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Christine Garcia  M D  Reports To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Calcifications  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA WITH MIXED LOBULAR AND DUCTAL FEATURES  SEE TABLE 1 AND NOTE   ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  At least 0 8cm  microscopic measurement   GRADE  1  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Positive along a broad front at the superior and inferior margins and focally positive at the posterior margin of the oriented specimen  and positive along a broad front at the inked margins of the unoriented soft tissue fragment   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  With immunohistochemical studies  the invasive tumor is positive for cytokeratin  confirming the diagnosis of carcinoma  The tumor exhibits variability in e cadherin staining  showing strong membranous staining in some areas and reduced to absent in others  especially where the carcinoma is composed of single file strands of tumor cells  Taken together  the morphologic and immunophenotypic features support the diagnosis of an invasive mammary carcinoma with mixed lobular and ductal features  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosi