Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 55 CLINICAL DATA  79 year old female with right breast cancer  Status post chemo x 5  Biopsy in REMOVED_DATE showed infiltrating ductal and lobular carcinoma with lobular carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  2  RESIDUAL LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  INFLAMMATORY REACTION TO SUTURE  CONSISTENT WITH SITE OF PREVIOUS SURGERY  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma is present in the form of single cells and small aggregates of cells percolating through stroma in multiple areas throughout the breast  An estimation of the overall size of the tumor is difficult  but it spans at least 5cm  Infiltrating tumor extends to within 0 1cm of the deep inked surface  An immunoperoxidase stain for keratin confirms the presence of infiltrating carcinoma  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   AXILLARY DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IS PRESENT IN FOURTEEN OF SIXTEEN LYMPH NODES  EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION IS PRESENT  NOTE  An immunoperoxidase stain for keratin confirms the presence of metastatic carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 41 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast with some axillary contents  is a right modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm  There is an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with a 3 0cm curved healed incision 3 0cm lateral to the unremarkable nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm firm tan white mass with areas of white streaking and a granular gritty cut surface  approximately 1 6cm inferior to the incision and extending to 0 5cm of the deep inked margin  Approximately 4 0cm medial to the lesion is a firm white area approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  grossly abutting the inked deep margin  The remainder of the parenchyma shows foci of firm white gritty tissue within areas of gray fibrous soft tissue  These areas of firm white gritty tissue are infiltrated with fat  The nipple is unremarkable  Multiple areas are sectioned and submitted as follows  Section Code  A  lesion  deep to scar  closest deep margin  0 5cm    B  lesion  C  lesion  D  lesion within 0 9cm of the deep margin  E  lesion  F G  firm white area abutting the inked deep margin  H  representative breast parenchyma  I J  fibrous area 2 0cm lateral to the lesion  K O  nodes from axillary tail  P  nodes and suspicious area in axillary tail  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  AND AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Unchecked.
