ning of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 MAY 97 at 15 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen SEction Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of breast tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink  firm  irregular mass with an eccentric round hemorrhagic area extending to the inked margin  Entirely submitted in A through J  with nodule in G through J  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST NODULE  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
