Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13 16 CLINICAL DATA  Ductal carcinoma in situ on prior core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SLIDE J  NEAR LOCALIZING WIRES   SEE TABLE AND NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 2  SOLID TYPE WITH COMEDONECROSIS AND INTERMEDIATE NUCLEAR GRADE  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  ADJACENT TO AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE ON 4 OF 10 SLIDES  E F G J   SEE TABLE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND CALCIFICATIONS  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  measured from slide J  Grade  2 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified Blood vessel invasion  Not identified Margin of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 1cm from the anterior margin of the specimen in one focus  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the invasive tumor mass Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 1cm from the anterior margin of the specimen in one focus  Stains for receptors  Requested NOTE  Immunostains for myoid and myoepithelial markers  p63  actin  calponin  heavy chain myosin  show an absence of myoepithelial cells around the invasive nests  which are admixed with nests of in situ tumor  The invasive component is present in just one section  J  away from the biopsy cavity  in the area designated as suspicious by radiographic study  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 20 00                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS