racteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm irregular portion of yellow tan fibrofatty soft tissue which is oriented with a short suture at the superior aspect and a long suture at the lateral aspect  It is inked as follows  black posterior medial  blue posterior lateral  green anterior lateral  red anterior medial  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal two firm  ill defined masses  Mass  1 is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm mass with a tan cut surface which is surrounded by white tan fibrous tissue  Mass  1 is located in the posterior medial quadrant of the specimen  centrally between superior to inferior poles  and extends to within 0 3cm of the posterior resection margin  to within 1 0cm of the medial resection margin  to within 0 8cm of the anterior resection margin  and is greater than 1 0cm away from the remaining resection margins  Mass  2 is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm mass with a tan and smooth cut surface located in the posterior region of the specimen approximately midway between the medial and lateral poles and approximately midway between the superior and inferior poles  It grossly extends to within 0 1cm of the posterior resection margin  to within 1 0cm of the lateral resection margin and is greater than 1 0cm from the remaining resection margins  Only a small amount of fibrosis is associated with mass  2 which is present lateral to the mass  The remaining parenchyma is composed of yellow fatty tissue without other focal lesions  Representative tissue is submitted as follows  Section code  A  Mass  1 and mass  2 to posterior margin  B C  Remainder of mass  1  D E  Remainder of mass  2  F G  Uninvolved parenchyma  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast posterior margin  is an irregular portion of yellow fibrofatty soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in greatest dimensions  The specimen is oriented with a suture designating the surface of the tissue which was furthest from the tumor  The sutured surface  surface furthest from tumor  is inked black  The opposite surface  surface closest to tumor  is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable cut surface without focal lesions  The tissue is submitted entirely as cassettes H O  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast final shaved margin  are multiple irregular fragments of yellow fibrofatty soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in aggregate  Sectioning reveals an unremarkable fatty cut surface without focal lesions  The tissue is submitted entirely as cassettes P T  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  POSTERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 49 CLINICAL DATA  Needle localized biopsy of breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  99    REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I OF III  EXTENDING WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   1    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA  MICROCYSTS  INTRALOBULAR FIBROSIS AND DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  No definite lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast biopsy containing a 1 2cm in diameter  firm  gritty nodule  0 1cm from the closest margin  Representative frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Nodule entirely submitted in cassettes A and B  with representatives of remaining parenchyma in C through F  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOSPY   report_end  , Checked.
