TOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab is a 24 x 17 x 7cm modified mastectomy specimen with an attached 20 x 6cm skin ellipse including a 3cm unremarkable light tan nipple  There is also an attached 5 x 4 x 3cm axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm ill defined light tan firm mass present 1 3cm from the inferior superficial margin  5cm inferior from the nipple  There is an additional REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm light tan irregular fibrotic area within the center of the specimen  A representative section of the tumor is frozen as FX 1 and saved for estrogen receptor studies  SECTION CODE  A  Inferior superficial margin  B  Nipple  C F  Sections of tumor  G  Section of fibrotic tissue  H L  Lymph nodes  Resident  Horace C  Wu  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Unchecked.
