Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 59 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT MASS   EXCISION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3    95     DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE   5    SEE NOTE  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma is 1 8cm in greatest diameter  The tumor approaches several inked surgical resection margins  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Immunohistochemical studies for estrogen and progestrogen receptors will be reported as an addendum  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 36     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 42     HER 2 Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm red and yellow firm nodule with loose connecting adipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm gritty tan mass with ill defined borders and focal calcifications which extensively involves one of the inked margins  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen and sent to Cox 5  The remaining tissue is submitted in cassettes A through L  Resident  ROSS C  WHEELER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA EXTENDING TO INKED RESECTION MARGINS  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD O R  Diagnos