ified  which are submitted as follows  Section code  A   one 0 8cm lymph node bisected  B   one 1 2cm lymph node  serially sectioned  C   one 0 6cm lymph node bisected  D   one 1 2cm lymph node  bisected  E   one 1 2cm lymph node  bisected  F G  one 2 5cm fatty lymph node  serially sectioned  H   five lymph nodes  REMOVED_DATE to 0 9cm  submitted whole  I   one 0 8cm lymph node bisected  J   multiple lymph nodes  REMOVED_DATE to 0 5cm  submitted whole  K   one 0 8cm lymph node  bisected  L M  one 1 5cm lymph node with fatty replacement  serially sectioned and submitted entirely  N   one potential 2 0cm lymph node trisected  O   one 2 5cm lymph node with fatty replacement  trisected  P   one 0 5cm lymph node  bisected  Q   one potential 0 5cm lymph node  trisected  R   one 2 0cm lymph node  serially sectioned  S T  one 1 5cm cavitary lymph node with hemorrhage  serially sectioned and entirely submitted  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm portion of breast oriented by the surgeon as follows  short stitch superior  long stitch infero lateral  bow tie medial  There is a central cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm which opens anteriorly  consistent with prior incision site  There is a firm area measuring approximately 2 0cm in dimension  located in the superio lateral aspect of the breast tissue adjacent to the anterior aspect of biopsy cavity  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  lateral yellow  This specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white  firm  stellate mass with an eccentric area of hemorrhage  The mass is located in the area of the previously described  firm region  and is located 0 5cm from the biopsy cavity  0 1cm from the anterior margin  1 0cm from the lateral margin and greater than 2 0cm from all other margins  The remainder of the specimen 