rially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm cavity containing dark red blood clot  which is consistent with previous biopsy site  The cavity is located in the lower outer quadrant and comes to 3 3cm of the posterior margin and 3 1cm of the anterior margin  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular  elongated  indurated  gray white mass in the mid breast tissue  which comes to 2 0cm of the posterior margin  4 8cm of the anterior margin  and is 1 8cm superomedial to the cavity  The mass cannot be cut with a blade due to probable calcifications  No other gross abnormalities are identified  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals several possible tan red lymph nodes  averaging 0 3cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  entirely submitted   following decalcification   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue between mass and cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity  with the posterior margin closest to the cavity as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved mammary tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper outer quadrant  which may represent lymph nodes  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  180   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of tan pink fibrofatty tissue  which is sectioned to reveal two tan pink lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The former is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the latter is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMYLYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SE , Unchecked.
