Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 33 CLINICAL DATA  43 year old female with right breast cancer  right modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  SINGLE FOCUS JUST OUTSIDE THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  AWAY FROM MARGINS  SECTION E   THERE IS NO RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   REGIONAL NODE DISSECTION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITHIN 1 OF 17 LYMPH NODES  ENLARGED TO REMOVED_DATE CM DIAMETER  WITH AN AREA SUGGESTIVE OF EARLY EXTRACAPSULAR SPREAD  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph Node  Right Axilla   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Two specimens are received fresh  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  The first specimen consists of an unoriented  20 x 17 x 4cm radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying 19 x 10cm ellipse of skin with unremarkable nipple  There is an 11 x 8 x 2cm portion of tissue projected from the main specimen  presumablY the axillary tail  There is a 5cm  well healed  curvilinear biopsy site present 3 5cm superior to the nipple  Beneath this scar is a palpable  firm mass  The area over the mass is inked black  Cross sectioning reveals a large  4 x 7 x 3 5cm biopsy cavity filled with serosanguineous fluid  The tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity is very soft  yellow  and friable  The tissue surrounding the biopsy site on the superficial side is very firm  and appears to abut the overlying skin  This margin is in A  The biopsy cavity comes to within 1 2cm of the deep surface  The deep surface margin is in B  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity are in C E  The tissue away from the breast cavity appears unremarkable  Representative sections are in F and G  The axillary tail is dissected  revealing multiple lymph nodes which are bisected and half submitted in G K  One of the nodes is suspicious for metastatic carcinoma  with a very firm  homogeneous  white tan surface  This node is in I  Designated  right axillary nodes  are two tissue fragments measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Several lymph nodes are identified  bisected  and half submitted in J M  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 12 CLINICAL DATA  57 y o  female with h o invasive lobular carcinoma of the left breast                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN REMOVED_DATE LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  SKIN  LEFT MASTECTOMY EDGE   SEBORRHEIC KERATOSIS  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  THESE SLIDES WERE REVIEWED BY DR  A  ZEMBOWICZ  WHO CONCURS WITH THE DIAGNOSIS  Diagnosis by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 40                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm unoriented simple mastectomy specimen  Attached is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm skin ellipse  with a areola measuring 3 0cm in diameter and a nipple measuring 1 5cm in diameter  The skin ellipse is eccentrically located on the roughly ovoid mastectomy specimen  and to provide a frame of reference the side containing the skin ellipse will be arbitrarily designated  inferior  and the opposite side will be arbitrarily designated  superior   The skin ellipse is remarkable for a 2 4cm curvilinear  well healed scar along its inferior edge centrally  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm semilunar firm to hard lesion at the superior border of the ellipse  Otherwise  it is tan and unremarkable with no evidence of nipple or skin retraction  The external surface of the breast parenchyma is also unremarkable  The deep  posterior  margin is inked black and the anterior margin is inked blue  The tissue is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm biopsy cavity  filled with a viscous brown fluid  located subjacent to the scar noted on the skin ellipse  At its closest approach  the biopsy cavity extends to within 0 5cm of the deep margin and to within 0 6cm of the anterior margin  Surrounding the biopsy cavity is abundant firm white scar tissue which is focally yellow and gritty  These ill defined foci of yellow gritty material extend to and abut the deep margin  spanning a region measuring 2 2cm  Elsewhere  the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  The tissue is extensively searched for lymph nodes  but none is identified  SECTION CODE  A  biopsy cavity to closest deep margin B E  remaining biopsy cavity with surrounding yellow gritty scar tissue F G  scar tissue adjacent to biopsy cavity H  breast parenchyma away from biopsy cavity I  red lesion at superior border of skin ellipse Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  axillary nodes  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm portion of yellow fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from 0 3cm to 2 8cm in greatest dimension  They are submitted as cassettes J O  with cassette O containing a single lymph node sectioned  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  mastectomy margin skin edge  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm skin ellipse with a small amount of yellow fatty subcutis attached  excised to a depth of 0 6cm centrally  The skin is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nonpigmented  round  raised  well circumscribed lesion  No other lesions are identified  The specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely as cassettes P R  with the raised lesion in cassette R  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  W P Andrew Lee  M D  David Nathan Helman  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT  PART C  SKIN  LEFT MASTECTOMY EDGE  , Unchecked.
