Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 56 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM EXTENDING TO THE POSTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN  1  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FLORID  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN  2  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN  3  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA INVOLVING A SINGLE TERMINAL DUCT LOBULAR UNIT  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm oriented breast biopsy  The specimen is inked as follows  the medial half   black  lateral half   blue  posterior surface   green over blue or black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm in maximum diameter white gray firm stellate nodule abutting the posteromedial resection margin  A representative section of tumor with posteromedial margin is frozen as FX 1  now submitted in A  The tumor is entirely submitted in A D  Additional breast parenchyma is submitted in E H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  bisected and entirely submitted in I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   2  are two pieces of tan yellow fibroadipose breast tissue  each REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The pieces are submitted entirely in J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   3   are two pieces of tan yellow fibroadipose breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  respectively  Each is submitted in K and L  respectively  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA TO POSTERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnos