  RIGHT  ANTERIOR FINAL MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL FINAL MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  JOSEPH T  RABBAN  M D   M P H  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 12 56                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm oriented right breast lumpectomy specimen with a needle localization guide wire through the specimen  The exterior of the specimen is tan yellow adipose tissue and is inked anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  The specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm firm well defined tan white homogeneous appearing mass that abuts the inferior margin  is 0 6cm to the superior  0 7cm to the posterior margin  0 2cm to the anterior margin  2 0cm to the lateral margin  and 1 5cm to the medial margin  Representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes A D with the inferior margin in A B and remaining anterior  posterior and superior margins in A D  Sections away from tumor are submitted in cassettes E F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan pink lymph node that is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes G H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast final superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of adipose tissue with a stitch designating the side away from the tumor  The stitched side is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes I J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast final lateral margin  is a R