Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  31 AUG 98 at 10 42 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  REMOVED_DATE CM  MIXED MODERATELY AND POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MIXED HIGH AND INTERMEDIATE GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Definite angiolymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The moderately differentiated tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The moderately differentiated tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The poorly differentiated tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  Rare poorly differentiated tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 37     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The poorly differentiated tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 06 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  R breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm unoriented piece of fibroadipose tissue and a second smaller REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm  tan lesion in the parenchyma that abuts the resection margin on several aspects  A second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm ill defined  firm tan lesion is present  also abutting the resection margin  the two masses appear contiguous  The first lesion is entirely submitted in A  The second lesion is entirely submitted in B C  The small fragment of fibroadipose tissue is bisected and submitted entirely in D  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
