aining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm portion of fibrofatty tissue  with a suture marking the deep margin  The specimen is entirely inked black and the area with the stitch is over inked green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a firm stellate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm mass which is within 0 2cm grossly of the closest  deep  margin  A representative section of the deep margin is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in toto in cassettes A   H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue one of which has a stitch  noted to be  posterior margin    and is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The other two fragments are unoriented  yellow fatty tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  respectively  All three specimens are inked black  the stitch surface is double inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal tan to white fibrous tissue grossly abutting the margin in the specimen with a stitch  and unremarkable adipose tissue in the other fragments  Section Code  I K  serial sections from the specimen with the stitch  submitted entirely  L  representative section from the second fragment  M  third  smallest fragment  submitted entirely  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  DEEP MARGIN  