nd eosin stained section  other immunostained sections  or still deeper sections that were subsequently obtained  Adjacent to this focus of microinvasive carcinoma is a second focus of ductal carcinoma in situ that is grade 1  A topographically separate second focus of ductal carcinoma in situ in the same section is grade 3  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Wyatt  REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a 21 x 20 x 3cm oriented left simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating axillary portion of the specimen  The anterior surface bears a 19 x 6cm tan brown skin ellipse  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple which are grossly unremarkable  There is a 2 5cm linear well healed scar present approximately between 1 and 3 o clock position  3cm from the areola in the outer quadrant  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially bread loafed to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm fibrotic  calcified scar approximately between 1 and 3 o clock position in the outer quadrant beneath the overlying linear well healed scar on skin which lies 0 3cm from posterior and 2 4cm from overlying margin  Approximately 7cm medial to this scar there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm biopsy cavity approximately between 6 and 7 o clock position  The biopsy cavity is lined a glistening lining and contain hemorrhagic material and a clip  The biopsy cavity lies 0 6cm from posterior and 5cm from overlying anterior inked margin  The breast parenchyma between the scar and the biopsy cavity contains predominantly tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue interspersed with a moderate amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma contains a moderate amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue admixed with tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  No additional discrete mass or lesion is grossly appreciated  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  calcified scar  located between 1 and 3 o clock in the outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire biopsy cavity located between 6 and 7 o clock   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  breast parenchyma intervening the scar and the biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  breast parenchyma  inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  breast parenchyma  outer quadrant  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 06 51PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  Amendment  1 by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Thursday February 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 07 52AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The invasive tumor cells and the adjacent ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  grade 1  stain for estrogen receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for progesterone receptor protein and HER 2 c erbB 2 do not show the invasive tumor cells or the adjacent ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  grade 1   The second focus of ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  grade 3  do not stain for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins  and HER 2 c erbB 2  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor ce