FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Sections of the main lumpectomy specimen reveal an invasive carcinoma with a main tumor mass measuring 1 7cm in maximum diameter  In addition to this main mass  there are many microscopic satellite nodules present suggesting a larger overall mass than the 1 7cm measured grossly  The tumor exhibits two distinct growth patterns  In some areas there is a distinct single file growth pattern characteristic of invasive lobular carcinoma  In other areas  the tumor infiltrates in small angulated nests  typical of tubular carcinoma  Immunohistochemical stains for e cadherin were performed on blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The e cadherin stain is negative in areas of invasive lobular growth pattern and positive in areas of tubular growth pattern  The e cadherin stain is also negative in areas of LCIS and positive in areas of DCIS  The immunohistochemical staining pattern supports the morphologic findings  Thus the overall impression is that of an invasive tubulo lobular carcinoma  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  LYMPH NODE  LEFT NON SENTINEL AXILLARY   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE  0 1   BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN SUPERIOR LATERAL   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE TUBULO  LOBULAR CARCINOMA PRESENT AT THE MARGIN OF RESECTION  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE   Note  An immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin is negative in areas of invasive and in situ lobular carcinoma and supports the diagnosis  Multiple level sections were examined  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross descriptions  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN INFERIOR LATERAL   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE TUBULO  LOBULAR CARCINOMA  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  INVASIVE TUBULO LOBULAR CARCINOMA IS 