_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary nodes  are two fragments of fibrofatty tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The smaller fragment appears to contain two potential lymph nodes  Each fragment is bivalved and the specimen is submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue containing a potential lymph node  The specimen is bivalved and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node 175  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragmented fibrofatty tissue with a single 0 5cm potential lymph node which is bivalved and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The rest of the tissue is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node 460  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm potential lymph node which is bivalved and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL  REMOVED_CASE_ID    EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL 175   EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL 160   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 39 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90   REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 3  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10   SOLID AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  ADJACENT TO AND AT A DISTANCE FROM THE MAIN TUMOR MASS  PRESENT AT AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  Areas of comedo type necrosis are present within the main tumor mass and may indicate comedocarcinoma in situ overgrown by infiltrating carcinoma  Foci of ductal carcinoma in situ away from the main tumor show high grade cytological features  but no comedonecrosis  The intra operative touch preparation diagnosis is confirmed  Hormone receptor protein stains will be performed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 38                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm pink tan to yellow firm fragment of breast tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm well defined red brown granular mass with scattered yellow nodules  abutting inked resection margins  The remaining parenchyma is white  firm  and soft yellow  A touch prep of the lesion is done  No frozen section is done  Representative sections are submitted in A H  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     TOUCH PREP DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST   POSITIVE FOR MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D  O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Douglas B  Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Checked.
