Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 30 CLINICAL DATA  Patient with history of lymphoma on FNA of breast nodule                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  HIGH GRADE B CELL LYMPHOMA  NOTE  The lymphoma is composed of medium sized cells with round to irregular nuclei and a moderate amount of cytoplasm  The cells are smaller than those of typical large cell lymphoma and in areas resemble those of Burkitt like lymphoma  However the mitotic rate  while high  is less than typical Burkitt like lymphoma and  starry sky  histiocytes are not prominent  In addition  the Ki67 proliferation marker is positive in 50 70  of tumor cells  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D  Signed On  04 MAY 98 at 13 56                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibody to B lineage  antigen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are negative for antibody to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to T lineage associated antigens  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of cells scattered within the tissue  The cells are also positive for Ki 67 in approximately 50 70  of the cells  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of B cell lymphoma  Added by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D  Signed On  05 MAY 98 at 18 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast nodule   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate of tan pink to brown soft tissue  one half submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   now in cassette A  The remainder is submitted in cassette B  Gross Description by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Mark J Ott  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 33 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT MASS  1   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  The carcinoma is less than 0 1cm from the closest resection margin  No lymphatic or venous invasion is noted  BREAST  LEFT MASS  2   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  MASS  1   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 25     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two separate specimens  Labeled  left breast   1    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 2cm in greatest diameter  well circumscribed  stellate  hard nodule that abuts the inked margin  A representative section of this nodule is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Entirely submitted in cassettes in A through F  with nodule in cassettes A through C  Labeled  left breast   2    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal no areas suspicious for carcinoma  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes G through P  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST  1  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  2  NO GROSS LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST MASS PART B  LEFT BREAST MASS  2 , Unchecked.
