iopsy cavity is present in the outer quadrant approximately beneath the linear scar on the overlying skin between 7 00 and 10 o clock position  is lined by tan yellow  smooth to focally polypoid lining and contains hemorrhagic fluid  The biopsy cavity lies 0 6cm from overlying skin and 1 5cm from posterior inked margin  The second biopsy cavity in the central quadrant lies approximately beneath the semicircular scar on overlying areola  2 5cm medial to the first cavity in the outer quadrant and measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The cavity is lined by tan yellow to hemorrhagic irregular lining  lies 0 6cm from overlying skin and 7 5cm from posterior inked margin  The breast parenchyma between these two biopsy cavities contains tan white  rubbery and nodular fibrous breast parenchyma  The remaining breast parenchyma contains predominantly tan yellow lobulated cut surface interspersed with scant fibrous tissue  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  Five possible lymph nodes dissected ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to 1x 1 x o 4cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  biopsy cavity of outer quadrant to include closest anterior and posterior inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  biopsy cavity of central quadrant to include closest anterior and posterior inked margin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous nodular breast parenchyma intervening of the two biopsy cavities   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous breast parenchyma  upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous breast parenchyma  inner lower quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single possible lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single possible lymph node  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTO